# MASTER AWS — 12 Essential AWS Services

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
| No. | AWS Service                  | Purpose                                                                        |
| --- | ---------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| 01  | Amazon EC2                   | Provides virtual servers to run applications                                   |
| 02  | Amazon S3                    | Stores files, images, backups, and other objects                               |
| 03  | AWS IAM                      | Manages users, roles, permissions, and access control                          |
| 04  | Amazon VPC                   | Creates an isolated virtual network for AWS resources                          |
| 05  | Amazon EBS                   | Provides persistent block storage for EC2 instances                            |
| 06  | Elastic Load Balancing (ELB) | Distributes incoming traffic across multiple targets                           |
| 07  | EC2 Auto Scaling             | Automatically adjusts the number of EC2 instances based on demand and policies |
| 08  | Amazon Route 53              | Provides DNS, domain routing, and health-check capabilities                    |
| 09  | Amazon RDS                   | Manages relational databases such as PostgreSQL and MySQL                      |
| 10  | Amazon DynamoDB              | Provides a managed NoSQL key-value and document database                       |
| 11  | AWS Lambda                   | Runs code without managing servers                                             |
| 12  | Amazon EKS                   | Runs and manages Kubernetes workloads on AWS                                   |
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

